      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The theory of defect-mediated melting gave a powerful, general account of phase transitions in two dimensions and predicted the hexatic phase. Its conceptual reach across condensed matter and soft matter is exceptional.",
        "attribution": "Halperin, Nelson, and Young are appropriately credited for the central theory and its development.",
        "maturity": "The framework has had decades of scrutiny and broad influence; its core conclusions are well established.",
        "uncertainties": [
